 [17592186516264 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4a73e654-74cd-553c-bd37-5755a05e3bca" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516360 #edb/ref 1080 "3x+6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516360 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516360 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6f9a04e1-a076-5063-b000-58d0bd6211f0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516458 #edb/ref 1080 "3x-8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516458 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516458 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a5683896-77cb-5f32-b1ff-4d08b73452cb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516703 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186516172 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516703 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186516254 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516703 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186516264 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516703 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186516360 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516703 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186516458 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516703 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516703 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516703 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186516264 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516703 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "70dfe391-1be5-5314-819b-7419c185891e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516867 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186516703 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516867 #edb/ref 1069 "q-163132" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516867 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516867 #edb/ref 1071 "For the function $f:{R}^{2}\\to R,$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x-y),\n$$\n\nthe quadratic Taylor polynomial of $f$ about $a=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈∗+[\\begin{aligned}∗ & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}∗ \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{1}{2}{[\\begin{aligned}∗ \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}∗ & 3 \\\\ ∗ & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the sum of the six missing expressions." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516867 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f8fd8fac-7611-58e8-a16a-eb7f95407000" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516867 #edb/ref 1074 "Suppose that the function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ is defened by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶z\n$$\n\n \n\nand is twice differentiable at $x=a.$ Then, the quadratic Taylor polynomial of $f$ about $a$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ≈f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a)+\\frac{1}{2}(x-a)^{T}{f}^{″}(a)(x-a),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(a)={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}]|}_{x=a}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(a)={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}]}_{x=a}\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}], & \\,{f}^{″}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the terms of our Taylor polynomial:\n\n- Calculating the value of the function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0,0) & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Calculating the first derivatives, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x-y) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x-y)\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {f}^{′}(0,0) & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Calculating the second derivative, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}-9\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x-y) & 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x-y) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x-y) & -\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x-y)\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {f}^{″}(0,0) & =[\\begin{aligned}-9 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the second-degree Taylor polynomial is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈1+[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{1}{2}{[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}-9 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFinally, the sum of the missing expressions is\n\n$$\n1+0+x+x+(-9)+3=2x-5.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516874 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186516972 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516874 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "02df79de-1a4d-5335-b5b6-f27a07496e01" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516874 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186284521 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516896 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186516925 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516896 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4115843a-5f65-5106-84b6-76017adc7761" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516896 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186281607 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516911 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186516874 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516911 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "61d3b2c9-87d8-5d72-b2fc-bc5dc51aac62" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516911 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186198678 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516925 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186516911 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516925 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7d2357c9-6ba0-5690-b808-3580c8ab9687" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516925 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186516867 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516972 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "da8884f4-3bad-5c57-9954-af1f3e1ee6f0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516972 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186367908 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
